# Thread — ${ticket}

Shared communication log for multi-agent work on this ticket.
Append-only. Each agent reads the tail before acting; appends one entry when done.

## Roles

The user assigns the agents at the start of the work by filling in the Agent
column. Use the agent's CLI or model name, such as Claude, Codex or Copilot.
Either agent can take either role.

| Role | Agent | Does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Writer | <agent> | Runs contract, plan, implement, approved fixes and closeout; edits code and workflow files. |
| Reviewer | <agent> | Reviews contract, plan and implementation with `independent-review`, and runs Gate D (`run review`). Appends findings to `thread.md`; never edits code. Gate D also writes `review.md`, `pull-request.md` and `workflow/.active-workflow.md`. |
| User | User | Approves each stage; picks which findings to fix. |

If your agent name isn't in the table, or the table still shows `<agent>`, write
`Question for User:` asking for your role, and stop.

The Reviewer joins at the stages where the Writer requests review (contract,
plan and implementation), not only at the final code review.

## Rules

- **Append only.** Head each entry `## <Agent> (<Role>) — YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM`, such as `## Claude (Writer) — 2026-11-11 13:55`. Take the time from the clock (`date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M'`) when you append; never estimate it. The user heads entries `## User — YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM`. Never edit earlier entries.
- **"your turn"** means: read every entry since your last one, do your part, append one entry, stop.
- **Writer entry:** what was done, files changed, commit SHA if any, what the Reviewer should check.
- **Reviewer entry:** numbered findings labeled BLOCKER, SHOULD FIX, or NICE TO HAVE, each with `file:line`. Otherwise "No findings." Report only real problems against the contract. No style comments, no extra features.
- **Writer fixes only findings the user approves.**
- **End every entry with `Next: <Role> — <what>`.**
- **At most two review rounds per stage.** Then write `Ready for User` and stop.
- **Ask, don't guess.** Unclear requirement or setup detail → write `Question for User:` and stop.

